      "options": "Extra Diligence",
      "ironing": "yes",
      "ironing_notes": "Inside out on cotton heat if you want that crisp, buttoned-up look. Steam it.",
      "iron_setting": "3",
      "drying": "Hang by the waistband and air dry. A hot dryer shrinks them and torches the elastane — an unforced error.",
      "colour_group": "dark",
      "mix_tags": "dye-bleeder",
      "notes": "Inside out, zips and buttons closed. Wash them far less than your instincts say — restraint is a growth strategy too.",
      "reference_name": "",
      "reference_link": ""
    },
    {
      "clothing_type": "Raw Denim (Founder Mode)",
      "detergent": "A capful of pH-neutral or denim-specific detergent. No bleach, no enzymes — zero-compromise, bootstrapped.",
      "fabric_softener": "no",
      "temperature": "cold",
      "spin": "400",
      "duration": "~0:45",
      "program": "High-Touch / Silk",
      "options": "",
      "ironing": "no",
      "ironing_notes": "Aligning this sets creases in the wrong places and flattens fades you spent months earning — respect the journey.",
      "iron_setting": "",
      "drying": "Hang inside out indoors, away from sun and radiators. Never tumble — protect the moat.",
      "colour_group": "dark",
      "mix_tags": "solo|dye-bleeder",
      "notes": "Unwashed denim is meant to go months before its first wash — patience is the whole strategy. Gentler than the machine: a 45-minute cold soak in the bath, inside out, no agitation, no wringing — then roll in a towel to press the water out.",
      "reference_name": "",
      "reference_link": ""
    },
    {
      "clothing_type": "Merino Wool (High Trust, Low Maintenance)",
      "detergent": "Wool detergent, half dose. No enzymes, no proteases, no bleach — they eat the fibre, a genuine existential risk.",
      "fabric_softener": "no",
      "temperature": "30",
      "spin": "400",
      "duration": "~0:40",
      "program": "Wool (Premium Tier)",
      "options": "",
      "ironing": "yes",
      "ironing_notes": "Only if you absolutely must: pressing cloth, no weight. Hanging it in a steamy bathroom drops the creases with zero effort — a real force multiplier.",
      "iron_setting": "2",
      "drying": "Never tumble dry. Dry flat on a towel, away from radiators and sun — hung up it stretches out and the regression is permanent.",
      "colour_group": "any",
      "mix_tags": "",
      "notes": "Turn inside out, wash with wool only, nothing with zips. Merino barely needs washing — air it overnight and redeploy it the next day. Efficient by design.",
      "reference_name": "",
      "reference_link": ""
    },
    {
      "clothing_type": "Synthetic Activewear (Hustle Culture)",
      "detergent": "A small dose of mild pH-neutral liquid detergent. Overdoing it is exactly what makes them smell — less is more, a genuine paradox.",
      "fabric_softener": "no",
      "temperature": "30",
      "spin": "800",
      "duration": "~1:10",
      "program": "Hustle Mode",
      "options": "Extra Diligence",
      "ironing": "no",
      "ironing_notes": "Elastane starts degrading around 110 °C, and the technical finish goes with it — skip alignment entirely.",
      "iron_setting": "",
      "drying": "Air dry on a hanger — dry within the hour, fast turnaround. Tumble heat kills the stretch for good.",
      "colour_group": "sport",
      "mix_tags": "lint-magnet",
      "notes": "Inside out. Never the softener culture-add: it films over the fibres these rely on for wicking and stretch. A cup of white vinegar in the rinse resets a load that's already gone stale. Covers tops, shorts and base layers — one fabric family, one sprint. Mixed colours are fine in one run: at 30 °C the dyes on polyester barely move. The exception is a brand-new black or strong red piece — onboard that one solo for a wash or two first.",
      "reference_name": "",
      "reference_link": ""
    },
    {
      "clothing_type": "Gym Socks",
      "detergent": "Liquid detergent, normal dose",
      "fabric_softener": "no",
      "temperature": "40",
      "spin": "1200",
      "duration": "~1:20",
      "program": "Hustle Mode",
      "options": "Extra Diligence",
      "ironing": "no",
      "ironing_notes": "",
      "iron_setting": "",
      "drying": "Tumble dry low or line dry.",
      "colour_group": "sport",
      "mix_tags": "lint-shedder",
      "notes": "Give them a 60 °C reset sprint every few weeks — 40 °C keeps them clean but doesn't actually reset the smell, just masks the metric.",
      "reference_name": "",
      "reference_link": ""
    },
    {
      "clothing_type": "Cashmere Blend (Premium Tier)",
      "detergent": "Wool or cashmere detergent, half dose. No enzymes, no proteases, no bleach.",
      "fabric_softener": "no",
      "temperature": "30",
      "spin": "400",
      "duration": "~0:40",
      "program": "Wool (Premium Tier)",
      "options": "",
      "ironing": "yes",
      "ironing_notes": "Low heat through a pressing cloth. Better still, steam it on a hanger and let the creases resolve themselves — passive alignment, my favorite kind.",
      "iron_setting": "2",
      "drying": "Never tumble dry. Squeeze the water out, never wring, then dry flat on a towel away from any heat.",
      "colour_group": "any",
      "mix_tags": "",
      "notes": "Inside out, and only ever with other wool — no cross-pollination. Cashmere pills where it rubs — that's the fibre behaving as designed, not a bug; a cashmere comb resolves it. Check the blend first: a little nylon adds resilience, silk adds fragility — know your inputs.",
      "reference_name": "",
      "reference_link": ""
    },
    {
      "clothing_type": "Wool Trainers (Niche but Passionate Fanbase)",
      "detergent": "A small amount of mild detergent — a wool detergent is ideal. No bleach.",
      "fabric_softener": "no",
      "temperature": "cold",
      "spin": "400",
      "duration": "~0:40",
      "program": "Wool (Premium Tier)",
      "options": "",
      "ironing": "no",
      "ironing_notes": "",
      "iron_setting": "",
      "drying": "Air dry only, somewhere with airflow: outside, by a window, or in front of a fan. Never the dryer, never a radiator — heat warps the sole and the regression is permanent.",
      "colour_group": "any",
      "mix_tags": "solo",
      "notes": "Pull the insoles and laces out first and wash those by hand — decouple the components. The shoes go in a mesh delicates bag or a pillowcase, solo — a loose trainer batters the drum and everything in it, a real blast-radius problem.",
      "reference_name": "",
      "reference_link": ""
    },
    {
      "clothing_type": "Linen (Timeless, On-Brand)",
      "detergent": "Mild liquid detergent, no bleach — bleach yellows linen and breaks the fibre down over time.",
      "fabric_softener": "no",
      "temperature": "40",
      "spin": "800",
      "duration": "~1:45",
      "program": "Low-Lift",
      "options": "Low-Effort Alignment",
      "ironing": "yes",
      "ironing_notes": "Align while still damp, as hot as the iron goes. Steam first to drop the worst of the creases before alignment even starts — front-load the easy wins.",
      "iron_setting": "max",
      "drying": "Line dry, or tumble on low and pull it out a little damp — bone dry in the machine is what locks the creases in for good.",
      "colour_group": "any",
